# PostGIS's regression tests whose outcome on versioned tables differs
# from heap's (t/299_postgis_regress.pl): one per line,
#
#	TEST MODE ISSUE KIND DIFF REASON...
#
# TEST as run_test.pl names it (regress/core/affine), MODE one of prolly,
# prolly_txn or prolly_dump, ISSUE the issue that decided or will fix the
# difference, KIND intended (postgres_semantics: decided, documented) or
# bug (known_bug: reported, not yet fixed), DIFF the md5 of the test's diff
# on that mode as the summary prints it.  Only that diff is listed: a test
# whose diff changes is a regression again, and so is a listed test that
# agrees with heap, so a fixed bug's line must go with its fix.

# Geometries PostGIS's text input accepts and its binary receive refuses
# (a one-point LINESTRING; unclosed rings) can't be committed.
regress/core/tickets prolly_txn #868 bug f9907ce93f5016ed1463575196e0d49d a one-point LINESTRING (#2985)
regress/core/clean prolly_txn #868 bug ee35342c6340bd6cc15f69e0118ed15e invalid polygons and lines
